<NAME>FPIF private markets split.</NAME>
<CONTENT>In FPIF’s February 2023 RFP, the fund says it is constructing a long-term target allocation of 31% to private market asset classes.

That 31% target is split as follows:
- 10% to private equity
- 7% to private debt
- 10% to real estate
- 4% to infrastructure

The RFP also specifies an additional detail for real estate and infrastructure:
- Of the 10% real estate target and 4% infrastructure target, 50% is intended for core open-ended vehicles
- The remaining 50% is intended for non-core commitments

So, in short, FPIF’s long-term private markets buildout is 31% total, allocated across private equity, private debt, real estate, and infrastructure in a 10% / 7% / 10% / 4% split.</CONTENT>
