[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The Arizona PSPRS RFP for non-discretionary investment consultant services evaluates proposals using four weighted criteria. The weights are explicitly stated in the RFP and apply to written submissions and, if held, finalist interviews.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>PSPRS RFP scoring weights.</NAME>
<CONTENT>Arizona PSPRS uses the following evaluation criteria and weights in its RFP for non-discretionary investment consultant services:

1. 25% — Relevant knowledge and experience  
   - Relevant knowledge and experience in similar consulting engagements  
   - Current organizational capacity to provide experienced staff  
   - Ability to perform the services described in the Scope of Services

2. 30% — Quality and extent of firm capabilities  
   This is the most heavily weighted category. It covers the firm’s capabilities in:
   - Strategic advice  
   - New investment identification and evaluation  
   - Operational due diligence  
   - Investment due diligence  
   - Manager performance reporting and monitoring  
   - Back office support

3. 25% — Demonstrated ability to meet service requirements  
   This includes:
   - Ability to communicate with the CIO and investment team  
   - Ability to communicate with Trustees and the Board’s consultant  
   - Responsiveness on ongoing and special issues  
   - Operational plan for fulfilling duties  
   - Quality of professional staff assigned to the contract

4. 20% — Overall cost  
   - Overall cost of the firm’s proposed services

Additional note from the RFP:
- Proposals are evaluated based on written submissions and/or finalist interviews.
- Interviews are not guaranteed, so firms are instructed to include all relevant information in their written proposals.</CONTENT>
[role=assistant] <SUMMARY>
# Markdown Briefing: Arizona PSPRS RFP Evaluation Criteria and Weights

Arizona Public Safety Personnel Retirement System (**PSPRS**) evaluates proposals for **non-discretionary investment consultant services** using **four weighted criteria**:

## Evaluation Criteria and Weights

- **25% — Relevant knowledge and experience**
  - Experience in similar consulting engagements
  - Organizational capacity to provide experienced staff
  - Ability to perform the services in the Scope of Services

- **30% — Quality and extent of firm capabilities**
  - Strategic advice
  - New investment identification and evaluation
  - Operational due diligence
  - Investment due diligence
  - Manager performance reporting and monitoring
  - Back office support

- **25% — Demonstrated ability to meet service requirements**
  - Communication with the CIO and investment team
  - Communication with Trustees and the Board’s consultant
  - Responsiveness on ongoing and special issues
  - Operational plan for fulfilling duties
  - Quality of professional staff assigned

- **20% — Overall cost**
  - Total proposed cost of services

## Key Takeaways

- The **most heavily weighted factor** is **quality and extent of firm capabilities (30%)**.
- **Experience** and **ability to meet service requirements** are each weighted at **25%**.
- **Cost** accounts for **20%** of the total evaluation.

## Evaluation Process Note

- PSPRS evaluates proposals based on **written submissions and/or finalist interviews**.
- Because **interviews are not guaranteed**, firms are expected to include all relevant information in their **written proposals**.
</SUMMARY>
