[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The IMRF sample RFP requires the investment consultant to attend a defined set of meetings with Board members and/or staff. The RFP also gives IMRF’s estimate of the total annual meeting time required.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>Required IMRF Meetings</NAME>
<CONTENT>Under the IMRF sample RFP for investment consulting, real estate consulting, and performance measurement services, the investment consultant must attend the following meetings with IMRF Board members and/or staff, on-site and off-site:

1. Monthly IMRF Board meetings  
2. Investment Committee meetings  
3. Annual IMRF Roundtable  
4. Regional meetings with investment managers  
5. Related investment meetings and discussions  
6. Formal interviews with existing and potential investment managers  
7. Ad hoc due diligence meetings with investment managers and Staff  

IMRF states in the RFP that, to complete these activities, it estimates there will be sixty days of meetings annually with the Board of Trustees and/or members of the staff.

The RFP also adds that there will be frequent telephone discussions with Staff relating to all investment issues covered by the assignment.</CONTENT>
[role=assistant] <SUMMARY>
# IMRF Required Meetings Briefing

Under the **IMRF sample RFP** for **investment consulting, real estate consulting, and performance measurement services**, the investment consultant is required to attend the following meetings with **Board members and/or staff**, both **on-site and off-site**:

- **Monthly IMRF Board meetings**
- **Investment Committee meetings**
- **Annual IMRF Roundtable**
- **Regional meetings with investment managers**
- **Related investment meetings and discussions**
- **Formal interviews with existing and potential investment managers**
- **Ad hoc due diligence meetings with investment managers and Staff**

## Estimated Annual Meeting Time

IMRF estimates that these responsibilities will require **60 days of meetings per year** with the **Board of Trustees and/or staff**.

## Additional Note

The RFP also indicates there will be **frequent telephone discussions with Staff** on investment issues covered by the assignment.
</SUMMARY>
