[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The evidence directly answers the question in section 1.6.2 of the 2018 INREV Due Diligence Questionnaire for Non-Listed Real Estate Investment Vehicles. It specifies the exact expense ratio to be provided and the calculation bases required.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>Required expense ratio.</NAME>
<CONTENT>Under Fees and Expenses in the 2018 INREV Due Diligence Questionnaire for Non-Listed Real Estate Investment Vehicles, the manager must provide the INREV Total Expense Ratio (TER).

The questionnaire states:
- If the vehicle has not been launched, the manager should provide a forward-looking estimate of the INREV TER and explain how it has been calculated.
- If the vehicle is an existing vehicle, the manager should provide the INREV TER.

The TER must be provided on the following bases:
- based on NAV;
- based on GAV;
- with performance fees; and
- without performance fees.

If INREV TER is not used, the manager should instead provide a calculation in line with the INREV Fee and Expense Metrics / INREV TER methodology.</CONTENT>
