[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The fixed income investment management questionnaire asks the firm to state whether it offers certain administrative and reporting-related services and, for each, whether an additional fee applies and the approximate amount. The listed services are clearly identified in the “Administration” section of the questionnaire.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>Services and extra fees</NAME>
<CONTENT>In the SAA fixed income investment management services questionnaire, the firm is asked under the Administration section to indicate for each service whether it is offered and, if so, the approximate additional fee, if any.

The services listed are:

- Schedule D investment accounting
- Asset/liability management (dynamic financial analysis)
- Performance attribution
- Daily internet access of portfolio information
- SVO filing

The questionnaire presents these in a table with columns for:
- Service
- Service Offered? (Yes/No)
- Approximate Fee

So the firm is being asked to confirm whether it provides each of those five services and to note any additional fee incurred for each service, including the approximate amount.</CONTENT>
