[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>In the PRS-STL actuarial auditing services RFP, the mandatory minimum qualifications state that the principal actuary assigned to PRS-STL must have at least five years of professional actuarial experience. The same section also requires at least five years of experience testifying before legislative and administrative bodies.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>PRS-STL actuary requirement.</NAME>
<CONTENT>The PRS-STL RFP’s “Mandatory Minimum Qualifications” says the principal actuary assigned to provide services to PRS-STL must have a minimum of five (5) years of professional actuarial experience.

Relevant details from that section:
- The principal actuary must have at least five (5) years of professional actuarial experience.
- The principal actuary must also be:
  - an enrolled actuary,
  - a Member of the American Academy of Actuaries,
  - and an Associate of the Society of Actuaries,
  - with Fellowship in the Society of Actuaries preferred.
